>4) What is this Elbereth thing that everyone talks about?

Elbereth was an Elvenking of old (from Lord of Rings), I think.
But anyways, monsters respect his name and if you engrave it or 
write it on the ground, monsters will not bother you ( as long as you
stand on it !!). Question: what is the hand of Elbereth ?
Also, I have heard that the engraving trick has been removed in later 
versions... and beware, most people don`t spell to well.

>5) I read the way to detect what kinds of wands you have without using them up,
>   and to determine ring types by dropping them in the sink--but how do
>   you discover what kinds of potions or scrolls you have without using
>   identify scrolls?

I am not sure there is a method for potions (other than clear->water)
but scrolls are priced according to what they are, and your charisma.
The cheapest is Identify, then comes Enchant Weapon, then Remove Curse,
Enchant Armour, and blank paper, then the majority, then Punishment,
Charging, Genocide and Taming.




>6) Why am I asking all these questions instead of figuring them out on
>   my own?

Because you want to suceed without working for it. Although your
character may get to high levels the player (you) can only become better
through working at the game. This means long hard hours in front of the
keyboard (ha.ha.) but it is much more fun to discover these things on
your own. Maybe this can get you a head start, but it will spoil your
game to get too many spoilers.

